# ---- the drawn-weapon LOCO (P2b production, FOLK-BODY): what a fighter shows for 4 s after a swing or while a foe is near
# (anim.cpp: the drawn idle and walk are the ACTION part's variant 1, the drawn run its walk variant 2: P2b fix r1,
# B10-ARMED-RUN-ATLAS, so the RUN atlas holds only the sheathed run and stays in its 64 KB for armed looks; ACTION is
# baked for every fighter anyway, the only bodies that run drawn). The weapon
# hand holds the blade in a ready guard (arms `guard`, held `guard` on its grip: A3's recover facing right and left); the
# off hand swings free of the empty scabbard (arms `o*`); the hips sit a pixel low on the guard / drawn stance and breathe
# up a pixel. The walk and the run keep the sheathed clips' legs, plants, bob, hangs and hair, so they register the same.
clip idle D part action family sword variant 1
f armL=oidle armR=guard held=guard legs=drawn neck=rest sheath=drawn torso=rest bob=1
f armL=oidle armR=guard held=guard legs=drawn neck=rest sheath=drawn torso=rest
f armL=oidle armR=guard held=guard legs=drawn neck=rest sheath=drawn torso=rest bob=1 expr=blink
